Modify scripts/orchestrate-agents-v2.ts. ADD ONLY — do NOT rewrite, do NOT touch any existing logic. File is ~2980 lines. FP-007 risk: any rewrite corrupts it. Make exactly 3 surgical additions:
1. At imports section (top of file, after existing imports around line 56-57): add: import { logCodeFailure } from './lib/code-failure-logger';
2. At the FINAL supervisor rejection path (line ~2375-2380, after 'git reset --hard HEAD~1' and before 'MonotaskSM.release(task.agent, task.id, `rejected attempt ${attempt}`)'): add: logCodeFailure({ taskId: task.id, sprintId: (process.argv[2]||'').replace(/.*\//, '').replace('.json',''), agentId: task.agent, attemptNum: attempt, score: lastReview?.score||0, model: (task as any).model||'unknown', rejectionReason: lastReview?.summary||'supervisor rejected', issues: lastReview?.issues||[], failType: isTruncation ? 'truncation' : 'supervisor_rejected' });
3. At the QA gate rejection path (line ~2321, after 'git reset --hard HEAD~1' and before 'MonotaskSM.release(task.agent, task.id, `QA gate: ${qaResult.reason}`)'): add: logCodeFailure({ taskId: task.id, sprintId: (process.argv[2]||'').replace(/.*\//, '').replace('.json',''), agentId: task.agent, attemptNum: attempt, score: 0, model: (task as any).model||'unknown', rejectionReason: qaResult.reason, issues: [], failType: 'qa_gate' });
IMPORTANT: If you cannot find the exact line numbers, search for the string 'MonotaskSM.release(task.agent, task.id, `rejected attempt' and 'MonotaskSM.release(task.agent, task.id, `QA gate' to locate the insertion points. Add the logCodeFailure call ONE LINE BEFORE each MonotaskSM.release call. Do not change anything else.
